      "description": "Watch Norwich City vs West Bromwich Albion highlights and goals from Championship on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 15, 2026. The stage was set for a classic encounter as the Championship season moved into high gear. On August 15, 2026 , fans witnessed a match that prioritized tactical discipline for over an hour before erupting into a clinical display of finishing. A Gritty Battle of Attrition The first half was characterized by a dense midfield struggle, with neither side willing to commit too many players forward. The referee was kept busy as challenges flew in, leading to a yellow card for Nathaniel Phillips in the 31st minute. Despite several probes into the final third, the lack of a final ball meant that the goalkeepers remained largely untested. When the whistle blew for half-time, the deadlock remained intact, leaving the managers to rethink their strategies in the dressing room. Breaking the Resistance The second period began with an early booking for Ousmane Diakite in the 48th minute, signaling that the physical nature of the game had not subsided. However, the introduction of substitutes provided the necessary spark. In the 75th minute, the breakthrough finally arrived. Jimmy-Jay Morgan turned provider, finding Aune Selland Heggeboe in a dangerous position, and the latter made no mistake to put his side ahead. The goal forced a change in momentum, as the defensive walls finally started to crumble. A Late Flourish Seals the Victory As the clock ticked toward full-time, the game opened up significantly. In the 87th minute, Jimmy-Jay Morgan capped off a brilliant performance by scoring himself, thanks to an assist from Max O'Leary . The scoring was not over yet, as Mathias Kvistgaarden added a third goal in the 90th minute to put the result beyond any doubt. After nine minutes of added time, the final whistle confirmed a dominant conclusion to a hard-fought contest, leaving the home crowd in raptures."
